# Git workflow conventions

Follow these whenever creating branches, commits, or pull requests. Do not invent alternate formats.

## Starting work (required)

Always start from an up-to-date **`staging`**, then create a **new** branch for the work. Commit only on that branch.

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout staging
git pull origin staging
git checkout -b <type>/<short-kebab-description>
```

Rules:
- **Never** commit directly on `staging`, `main`, or `development`
- **Never** continue unrelated work on someone else’s or a stale feature branch — open a new branch from `staging`
- After commits, open a PR **into `staging`** (not `main`)
- Only create the branch/commit/PR when the user asks to commit or open a PR; still use this base/branch flow when they do

## Branch names

Pattern: `<type>/<short-kebab-description>`

Allowed types: `feature`, `bugfix`, `hotfix`, `chore`, `docs`, `ci`

Rules:
- Lowercase kebab-case only (`a-z`, `0-9`, `-`)
- Optional ticket: `feature/arc-123-hero-cta` or `feature/hero-cta`
- No spaces, underscores, or PascalCase

Examples:
- `feature/staging-netlify-deploy`
- `bugfix/mobile-nav-overflow`
- `chore/update-dependencies`
- `ci/add-pr-naming-checks`

### Merge targets

| From | Into | Notes |
|------|------|--------|
| `feature/*`, `bugfix/*`, `chore/*`, `docs/*`, `ci/*` | `staging` | Branched from `staging`; PR back to `staging` |
| `hotfix/*` | `staging` (prefer) or `main` only for prod emergencies | Still prefer branching from `staging` |
| `staging` | `main` | Only `staging` may PR into `main` |
| `development` | `staging` | Integration branch; does not deploy |

Never open a feature-branch PR directly into `main`.

## Commit messages

Use Conventional Commits:

```
<type>(optional-scope): <imperative summary>

Optional body — why, not what.
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `style`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`

Rules:
- Subject ≤ ~72 chars, imperative mood, no trailing period
- Focus on **why**; keep the body short
- Pass the message via HEREDOC when committing from the agent
- Do not commit unless the user asked

Examples:
- `feat(staging): deploy Netlify from Actions after merge`
- `fix: restore FAQ accordion on mobile`
- `ci: add PR and branch naming checks`
- `docs: document staging and production deploy flow`

## PR titles

Same shape as commits (ticket optional):

```
[TICKET-ID] type(scope): description
```

or without ticket:

```
type(scope): description
```

Examples:
- `[ARC-42] feat: add staging Netlify deploy workflow`
- `fix: correct GoDaddy .htaccess canonical redirects`
- `ci: enforce branch and PR title conventions`

## PR body

When opening or drafting a PR, use this structure (match `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`):

```markdown
## Summary
- 

## Test plan
- [ ] 

## Deploy notes
- Target branch: `staging` | `main`
- Staging → Netlify via Actions after merge (no issue gate)
- Main → production issue approval, then GoDaddy FTP
```

Fill Summary with 1–3 concrete bullets. Prefer a checklist in Test plan. Note env/secret or Netlify/GoDaddy impact under Deploy notes when relevant.
